      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(discord): bound webhook JSON response reads to prevent OOM",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`extensions/discord/src/send.webhook.ts:124` calls raw `response.json()` on the webhook POST response. Without a byte cap, a misbehaving or compromised webhook endpoint could return an arbitrarily large response, exhausting memory.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `send.webhook.ts`: replace unbounded `response.json()` with `readResponseWithLimit` (1 MiB cap) + `JSON.parse` with try/catch fallback\n- `send.webhook-bounded-json.test.ts`: 4 vitest tests that call the real `sendWebhookMessageDiscord()` with mocked fetch\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Vitest — exercises sendWebhookMessageDiscord directly\n\n```\npnpm exec vitest run extensions/discord/src/send.webhook-bounded-json.test.ts\n\n ✓ parses normal JSON webhook response\n ✓ rejects oversized webhook response exceeding the 1 MiB cap\n ✓ falls back to empty payload on empty success response\n ✓ falls back to empty payload on malformed JSON success response\n```\n\n### Call chain (production)\n\n`sendWebhookMessageDiscord(text, opts)` → `POST https://discord.com/api/webhooks/...` → `readResponseWithLimit(response, 1 MiB)` → `JSON.parse(body)` + try/catch fallback `{}` → `createDiscordSendResult`\n\n### Negative control\n\nReverting `readResponseWithLimit` to `response.json()` in the oversized test:\n- Before (main): `response.json()` buffers all 2 MiB → no error → unbounded OOM risk\n- After (PR): `readResponseWithLimit` rejects at 1 MiB → `Error: Discord webhook JSON response too large`\n\nLabel: security | merge-risk: 🟢 minimal | AI-assisted",
